    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d614">

                <pb facs="0970" n="954" sameAs="frus:frus1949v06/pg954"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">501.BB Palestine/4–2849</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum of Conversation With the President, by the
                        Secretary of State</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1949-04-28">April 28, 1949</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p rendition="#flush">
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Item No. 2—Letter from Dr. Weizmann</hi>
                </p>
                <p>The President showed me a letter from Dr. Weizmann,<anchor n="1" xml:id="d614-f1"
                    /> a copy of which will come to us today.</p>
                <p>The letter referred to a request that we assist by talking with other members of
                    the United Nations on the subject of admission of Israel to the United Nations.
                    The President agreed that Dr. Weizmann’s attitude on refugees was not
                    satisfactory and thought that we were not in a position to bring pressure on
                    other members of the United Nations.</p>
                <p>I related to the President my last meeting with Ambassador Elath and Mr.
                        Eban.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d614-f2"/>
                </p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
